  "scope": "The entire theorem of Federer 3.2.19, p. 256: almost everywhere on an H^m measurable finite-mass (H^m,m) rectifiable W, density of H^m restricted to W is one and its approximate tangent is exactly an m-dimensional Grassmann subspace. Every Lipschitz partial map with domain W has an approximate differential almost everywhere, with exactly that approximate tangent as partial domain. Each function may have its own exceptional set. The supporting chart theorem preserves the actual differential and exact partial precomposition identity. All natural dimensions, including zero, are retained.",
